{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"a97f52858bcb63a691493053","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c%40rong.moe/","channels":["lkml"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c@rong.moe","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c%40rong.moe/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c@rong.moe"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Check sticky mixers precisely","messages":{"1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe":{"id":"1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe","messageId":"1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe","references":["20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c@rong.moe","d62a54f6-c3dc-4502-b61c-6cdc49fe40f0@gmx.de"],"missingAncestorIds":["d62a54f6-c3dc-4502-b61c-6cdc49fe40f0@gmx.de","20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c@rong.moe"],"author":{"name":"Rong Zhang","address":"i@rong.moe"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Alexander Niemeyer","address":"adventureFAN@gmx.de"},{"name":"Jaroslav Kysela","address":"perex@perex.cz"},{"name":"Takashi Iwai","address":"tiwai@suse.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Takashi Iwai","address":"tiwai@suse.de"},{"name":"","address":"linux-sound@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T13:50:40.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T13:50:40.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Check sticky mixers precisely","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Alexander,"},{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Sun, 2026-08-16 at 07:14 +0200, Alexander Niemeyer wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Hi Rong,"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I tested the sticky-check part of your patch on the Logitech PRO X "},{"depth":1,"text":"Wireless (046d:0aba) on Fedora 44, kernel 7.1.8-200.fc44.x86_64."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Since your patch is based on a newer tree, I used a minimal backport of "},{"depth":1,"text":"the new ~16-value / 10 ms sticky-check logic to the 7.1.8 code. The "},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_CUR-broken handling from the newer tree was not included; GET_CUR "},{"depth":1,"text":"itself succeeds on this device."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Unfortunately, the playback control is still classified as sticky:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"2:0: sticky mixer values (-16384/0/256 => -3840), disabling"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I then instrumented the check and tried an additional diagnostic: after "},{"depth":1,"text":"every successful SET_CUR, wait 100 ms and perform another GET_CUR before "},{"depth":1,"text":"issuing the next SET_CUR."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"For the playback volume, the saved value was -3840 and GET_CUR remained "},{"depth":1,"text":"at -3840 for every tested value, even after 100 ms, for example:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"test=-15104 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"test=-13824 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"test=-3584 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"test=-2304 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"test=-1024 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"test=0 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"So in this case the issue does not appear to be simply that the "},{"depth":1,"text":"accumulated 10 ms sleeps are too short. During the probe-time sticky "},{"depth":1,"text":"check, SET_CUR succeeds but GET_CUR for the playback control remains "},{"depth":1,"text":"unchanged even when each SET_CUR is given 100 ms before the next one."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This differs from my previous direct libusb tests with the AudioControl "},{"depth":1,"text":"interface unbound, where valid SET_CUR values became visible through "},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_CUR after roughly 47–81 ms."}],"lineCount":36,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Really interesting. Maybe the mixer changes its value only when there is\nan opened playback stream."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Could you clarify your \"libusb tests\"?"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks,\nRong"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The first debug line I saw with |saved=0| was from the Mic Capture "},{"depth":1,"text":"Volume control; that control changed immediately and returned as "},{"depth":1,"text":"non-sticky. The sequence above with |saved=-3840| is the problematic PCM "},{"depth":1,"text":"Playback Volume control."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I'd be happy to test another version or run additional diagnostics if "},{"depth":1,"text":"useful."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Best regards,"},{"depth":1,"text":"Alexander"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Am 15.08.2026 um 23:47 schrieb Rong Zhang:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Some mixers are asynchronous, and some have broken min/max. They are"},{"depth":1,"text":"> mistakenly considered sticky due to how the check is implemented."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Check sticky mixers more precisely by checking approximately 16 values"},{"depth":1,"text":"> and adding a msleep(10) between each check, so that asynchronous mixers"},{"depth":1,"text":"> have enough time to change the value and mixers with broken min/max are"},{"depth":1,"text":"> checked properly. Additionally, mark GET_CUR as broken when"},{"depth":1,"text":"> get_cur_mix_raw() fails, instead of returning successfully."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Reported-by: Alexander Niemeyer <adventureFAN@gmx.de>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/r/6262cbbd-d1f2-4c9d-a1c7-9c5d12636f4b@gmx.de"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Signed-off-by: Rong Zhang <i@rong.moe>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> ---"},{"depth":1,"text":">   sound/usb/mixer.c | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------"},{"depth":1,"text":">   1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer.c b/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> index 703c118f9d4e..3d0f97730a06 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> --- a/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +++ b/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -1256,22 +1256,59 @@ static void init_cur_mix_raw(struct usb_mixer_elem_info *cval, int ch, int idx)"},{"depth":1,"text":">   static int check_sticky_volume_control(struct usb_mixer_elem_info *cval,"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t\t\t       int channel, int saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":">   {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\tint sticky_test_values[] = { cval->min, cval->max };"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\tint test, check, i;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tint test, check, res;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * Check approximately 16 values (15 intervals)."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * If the resolution is not fine enough, check fewer values."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tres = DIV_ROUND_UP(cval->max - cval->min, 15);"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tres = res ? roundup(res, cval->res) : cval->res;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * If (cval->max - cval->min) is not a multiple of cval->res, we still"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t * want to test cval->max anyway."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tfor (test = cval->min; test < cval->max + res; test += res) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tif (test > cval->max)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t\ttest = cval->max;"},{"depth":1,"text":">   "},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sticky_test_values); i++) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\t\ttest = sticky_test_values[i];"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\tif (test == saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t\tcontinue;"},{"depth":1,"text":">   "},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t/* Assume non-sticky on failure. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\t\tif (snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, channel, 0, test) ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\t\t    get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check) ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"> -\t\t    check != saved) /* SET_CUR effective, non-sticky. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tif (snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, channel, 0, test))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tif (get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t\tgoto get_cur_broken;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tif (check != saved) /* SET_CUR effective, non-sticky. */"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * Leave some time for asynchronous mixers to change the value."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t *"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * Note that there is no need to wait between SET_CUR and"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * GET_CUR, as we don't care whether the GET_CUR value matches"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * the SET_CUR one. IOW, what we expect is just a GET_CUR value"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * differing from the saved one."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t *"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * Mixers of most devices are synchronous. The should have"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * returned early without extra sleep. Asynchronous mixers will"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * return once the accumulated time is enough for them to change"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t * the value."},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tmsleep(10);"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":">   "},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t/* Check again after the last msleep(). */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tif (get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tgoto get_cur_broken;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tif (check != saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \tif (cval->head.mixer->chip->quirk_flags & QUIRK_FLAG_MIXER_GET_CUR_BROKEN) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +get_cur_broken:"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\tusb_audio_info(cval->head.mixer->chip,"},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t\t       \"%d:%d: broken mixer GET_CUR (%d/%d/%d => %d)\\n\","},{"depth":1,"text":">   \t\t\t       cval->head.id, mixer_ctrl_intf(cval->head.mixer),"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> ---"},{"depth":1,"text":"> base-commit: 3eb40771c00a8488fa6ed2cc1fe203477908bf38"},{"depth":1,"text":"> change-id: 74676fce-uac-precise-sticky-check-94474a22b57d"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Thanks,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Rong"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "}],"lineCount":109,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"d62a54f6-c3dc-4502-b61c-6cdc49fe40f0@gmx.de"},"6acbf6556133790ad093c5c4bb4a451526007e05.camel@rong.moe":{"id":"6acbf6556133790ad093c5c4bb4a451526007e05.camel@rong.moe","messageId":"6acbf6556133790ad093c5c4bb4a451526007e05.camel@rong.moe","references":["20260816-uac-precise-sticky-check-v1-1-00798373dc3c@rong.moe","d62a54f6-c3dc-4502-b61c-6cdc49fe40f0@gmx.de","1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe","74ca2e17-8fb8-4ede-8e7e-441be815b5b6@gmx.de"],"missingAncestorIds":["74ca2e17-8fb8-4ede-8e7e-441be815b5b6@gmx.de"],"author":{"name":"Rong Zhang","address":"i@rong.moe"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Alexander Niemeyer","address":"adventureFAN@gmx.de"},{"name":"Jaroslav Kysela","address":"perex@perex.cz"},{"name":"Takashi Iwai","address":"tiwai@suse.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Takashi Iwai","address":"tiwai@suse.de"},{"name":"","address":"linux-sound@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T15:08:08.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T15:08:08.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Check sticky mixers precisely","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hi Alexander,"},{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Sun, 2026-08-16 at 16:09 +0200, Alexander Niemeyer wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Hi Rong,"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Sure. The libusb tests were direct USB Audio Class 1 control transfers "},{"depth":1,"text":"to the headset using libusb/PyUSB, not ALSA mixer operations."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I accessed Feature Unit 2 on AudioControl interface 0, master channel 0, "},{"depth":1,"text":"with the UAC1 Volume control selector:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"wValue = 0x0200 /* Volume control, master channel */"},{"depth":1,"text":"wIndex = 0x0200 /* Feature Unit 2, interface 0 */"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I used the standard class-specific requests directly, including GET_CUR, "},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_MIN, GET_MAX, GET_RES and SET_CUR, with signed 16-bit little-endian "},{"depth":1,"text":"volume values in 1/256 dB units."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The device reported:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_CUR: 0 ( 0 dB in that test)"},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_MIN: -16384 (-64 dB)"},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_MAX: 0 ( 0 dB)"},{"depth":1,"text":"GET_RES: 256 ( 1 dB)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"For the timing tests I issued SET_CUR for a target value and then "},{"depth":1,"text":"repeatedly queried GET_CUR until the value changed or the timeout expired."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Valid values became visible after roughly:"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"-1 dB ~81 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":"-2 dB ~52 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":"-4 dB ~47 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":"-8 dB ~47 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":"-16 dB ~52 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":"-32 dB ~47 ms"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"The advertised -64 dB minimum behaved differently: SET_CUR returned "},{"depth":1,"text":"successfully, but GET_CUR did not change even after 1000 ms."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"To access the AudioControl interface with libusb, I unbound the "},{"depth":1,"text":"AudioControl interface from snd-usb-audio for the duration of the test."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"I did not intentionally open a playback stream during those libusb "},{"depth":1,"text":"tests. Because the AudioControl interface had been unbound from "},{"depth":1,"text":"snd-usb-audio, I also do not believe there was an active ALSA playback "},{"depth":1,"text":"stream at that point."}],"lineCount":44,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks for the information."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Unfortunately, I still don't exactly see why the device behaved\ndifferently when GET_CUR/SET_CUR requests were sent from snd-usb-audio\ncompared to your libusb tests."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"snd-usb-audio also tries SET_RES to test the sanity of GET_RES. Could you\ntest if it breaks your device's GET_CUR? "},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Maybe comparing them with usbmon can show some clues. You can use\nWireshark to sniff /dev/usbmon*. "},{"kind":"code","text":"Hint: a Thunderbolt port usually corresponds to a dedicated USB root hub."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"If you have one, plug the device to it to get pure usbmon trace results\nwith no noisy URBs from other devices."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Thanks,\nRong"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"If the open-stream state is important, I can repeat the experiment "},{"depth":1,"text":"specifically controlling for playback-stream-open versus "},{"depth":1,"text":"playback-stream-closed."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Thanks,"},{"depth":1,"text":"Alexander"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Am 16.08.2026 um 15:50 schrieb Rong Zhang:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Hi Alexander,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> On Sun, 2026-08-16 at 07:14 +0200, Alexander Niemeyer wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Hi Rong,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > I tested the sticky-check part of your patch on the Logitech PRO X"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Wireless (046d:0aba) on Fedora 44, kernel 7.1.8-200.fc44.x86_64."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Since your patch is based on a newer tree, I used a minimal backport of"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > the new ~16-value / 10 ms sticky-check logic to the 7.1.8 code. The"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > GET_CUR-broken handling from the newer tree was not included; GET_CUR"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > itself succeeds on this device."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Unfortunately, the playback control is still classified as sticky:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > 2:0: sticky mixer values (-16384/0/256 => -3840), disabling"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > I then instrumented the check and tried an additional diagnostic: after"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > every successful SET_CUR, wait 100 ms and perform another GET_CUR before"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > issuing the next SET_CUR."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > For the playback volume, the saved value was -3840 and GET_CUR remained"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > at -3840 for every tested value, even after 100 ms, for example:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=-15104 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=-13824 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=-3584 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=-2304 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=-1024 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > test=0 immediate=-3840 after100ms=-3840"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > So in this case the issue does not appear to be simply that the"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > accumulated 10 ms sleeps are too short. During the probe-time sticky"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > check, SET_CUR succeeds but GET_CUR for the playback control remains"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > unchanged even when each SET_CUR is given 100 ms before the next one."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > This differs from my previous direct libusb tests with the AudioControl"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > interface unbound, where valid SET_CUR values became visible through"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > GET_CUR after roughly 47–81 ms."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Really interesting. Maybe the mixer changes its value only when there is"},{"depth":1,"text":"> an opened playback stream."},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Could you clarify your \"libusb tests\"?"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> Thanks,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> Rong"},{"depth":1,"text":"> "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > The first debug line I saw with |saved=0| was from the Mic Capture"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Volume control; that control changed immediately and returned as"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > non-sticky. The sequence above with |saved=-3840| is the problematic PCM"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Playback Volume control."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > I'd be happy to test another version or run additional diagnostics if"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > useful."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Best regards,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Alexander"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > Am 15.08.2026 um 23:47 schrieb Rong Zhang:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Some mixers are asynchronous, and some have broken min/max. They are"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > mistakenly considered sticky due to how the check is implemented."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Check sticky mixers more precisely by checking approximately 16 values"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > and adding a msleep(10) between each check, so that asynchronous mixers"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > have enough time to change the value and mixers with broken min/max are"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > checked properly. Additionally, mark GET_CUR as broken when"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > get_cur_mix_raw() fails, instead of returning successfully."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Reported-by: Alexander Niemeyer<adventureFAN@gmx.de>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Closes:https://lore.kernel.org/r/6262cbbd-d1f2-4c9d-a1c7-9c5d12636f4b@gmx.de"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Signed-off-by: Rong Zhang<i@rong.moe>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > ---"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    sound/usb/mixer.c | 51 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    1 file changed, 44 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > diff --git a/sound/usb/mixer.c b/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > index 703c118f9d4e..3d0f97730a06 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > --- a/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +++ b/sound/usb/mixer.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > @@ -1256,22 +1256,59 @@ static void init_cur_mix_raw(struct usb_mixer_elem_info *cval, int ch, int idx)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    static int check_sticky_volume_control(struct usb_mixer_elem_info *cval,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t\t\t       int channel, int saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\tint sticky_test_values[] = { cval->min, cval->max };"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\tint test, check, i;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tint test, check, res;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t * Check approximately 16 values (15 intervals)."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t * If the resolution is not fine enough, check fewer values."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tres = DIV_ROUND_UP(cval->max - cval->min, 15);"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tres = res ? roundup(res, cval->res) : cval->res;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t * If (cval->max - cval->min) is not a multiple of cval->res, we still"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t * want to test cval->max anyway."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tfor (test = cval->min; test < cval->max + res; test += res) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tif (test > cval->max)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t\ttest = cval->max;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\tfor (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(sticky_test_values); i++) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\t\ttest = sticky_test_values[i];"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\tif (test == saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t\tcontinue;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t/* Assume non-sticky on failure. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\t\tif (snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, channel, 0, test) ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\t\t    get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check) ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > -\t\t    check != saved) /* SET_CUR effective, non-sticky. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tif (snd_usb_set_cur_mix_value(cval, channel, 0, test))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tif (get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t\tgoto get_cur_broken;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tif (check != saved) /* SET_CUR effective, non-sticky. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * Leave some time for asynchronous mixers to change the value."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t *"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * Note that there is no need to wait between SET_CUR and"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * GET_CUR, as we don't care whether the GET_CUR value matches"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * the SET_CUR one. IOW, what we expect is just a GET_CUR value"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * differing from the saved one."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t *"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * Mixers of most devices are synchronous. The should have"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * returned early without extra sleep. Asynchronous mixers will"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * return once the accumulated time is enough for them to change"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t * the value."},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tmsleep(10);"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t/* Check again after the last msleep(). */"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tif (get_cur_mix_raw(cval, channel, &check))"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\tgoto get_cur_broken;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\tif (check != saved)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \tif (cval->head.mixer->chip->quirk_flags & QUIRK_FLAG_MIXER_GET_CUR_BROKEN) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > +get_cur_broken:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\tusb_audio_info(cval->head.mixer->chip,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t\t       \"%d:%d: broken mixer GET_CUR (%d/%d/%d => %d)\\n\","},{"depth":1,"text":"> > >    \t\t\t       cval->head.id, mixer_ctrl_intf(cval->head.mixer),"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > ---"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > base-commit: 3eb40771c00a8488fa6ed2cc1fe203477908bf38"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > change-id: 74676fce-uac-precise-sticky-check-94474a22b57d"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Thanks,"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > Rong"},{"depth":1,"text":"> > > "}],"lineCount":164,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"74ca2e17-8fb8-4ede-8e7e-441be815b5b6@gmx.de","parentId":"1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe"}},"rootIds":["1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe"],"childrenByParent":{"1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe":["6acbf6556133790ad093c5c4bb4a451526007e05.camel@rong.moe"]},"chronologicalIds":["1abcec7c1a99e27f7d354ad35a36761099cfa587.camel@rong.moe","6acbf6556133790ad093c5c4bb4a451526007e05.camel@rong.moe"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}